From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: domicile CI <ci@domicile.invalid>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: the browser's clipboard is the desktop's

Copying in a terminal and pasting in a browser window did nothing, and so
did the other direction: the browser had a clipboard of its own that
nothing else on the desktop could reach.

`Clipboard::Create` asks the ozone platform for a `PlatformClipboard` and
falls back to `ClipboardNonBacked` -- an in-process store with no
connection to anything -- when there is none, and the DRM platform had
none. On a tty that is the whole of it: there is no display server for
the browser to share a clipboard through, so the fallback is what every
page, every text field and every <webview> guest was reading and writing,
while every Wayland client on the same desktop was reading and writing
the compositor's seat.

DrmClipboard is that missing one. It is not a store: the compositor is
the clipboard, and this is the browser's end of it. A copy made in a page
arrives at OfferClipboardData and is handed to the compositor, which puts
it on the seat every other window pastes from; a copy made anywhere else
arrives at SetContents, because the compositor reads every selection as
it is made -- so there is nothing left to fetch and a page pasting is
answered out of this process's memory.

BOTH CLIPBOARDS, because the desktop has two. IsSelectionBufferAvailable
answers yes, which is what makes a middle-click paste in a page ask for
the primary selection rather than be dropped before it reaches here.

IT IS NEVER THE SELECTION OWNER, including immediately after this process
copied. That answer is not about who copied: it is ClipboardOzone asking
whether it may serve a read out of its own cache of what it last offered,
and it may not, because the next copy on this desktop can be made in any
window and a browser reading its own cache would go on pasting what it
copied an hour ago.

The two new OzonePlatform entry points are how the compositor's
connection reaches this without //content/browser depending on //ui/ozone
internals or the reverse -- the same seam SetDomicileDisplayLayout uses,
for the same reason.

Nothing here is reached off the DRM platform. A nested run's browser is a
window inside somebody else's session and reads that session's clipboard,
which is a gap rather than a decision; see ROADMAP.md in the Domicile
repository.
---
 ui/ozone/platform/drm/BUILD.gn              |  3 +++
 ui/ozone/platform/drm/DEPS                  |  7 ++++++
 ui/ozone/platform/drm/ozone_platform_drm.cc | 28 +++++++++++++++++++++
 ui/ozone/public/ozone_platform.h            | 21 ++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 59 insertions(+)

